.TH REPLICA_FIX 1 "2026-10-02" "DUNE Rucio ops" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
replica_fix.sh \- clean up stale Rucio replica records on the DUNE tape-backed RSE
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B replica_fix.sh
.RB [ \-\-apply ]
.IR scope : name
.br
.B replica_fix.sh
.RB [ \-\-apply ]
.B \-\-list
.IR file | \-
.br
.B replica_fix.sh
.RB [ \-\-apply ]
.B \-\-dataset
.IR scope : name
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B replica_fix.sh
repairs replica rows in the
.B replicas
table of the production DUNE Rucio database
.RB ( dune_rucio_prod
on
.BR ifdb11.fnal.gov:5455 )
so that the Rucio reaper can remove them.
It acts only on replicas on the FNAL_DCACHE RSE
.RI ( rse_id
.BR a9780baa\-e23e\-4835\-9e2a\-84d3b19261ae ).
.PP
It is meant for files that were deleted from tape long ago but whose
replica records remain.
Such records often have a NULL
.BR path ,
which prevents the reaper from handling them.
.PP
For each target replica, two updates are applied:
.IP 1. 4
If
.B path
is NULL and
.B tombstone
is set,
.B path
is set to the placeholder
.BR /pnfs/dune/tape_backed/dunepro .
.IP 2. 4
If
.B lock_cnt
is 0 and
.B tombstone
is
.BR "1970\-01\-01 00:00:00" ,
.B state
is set to
.B A
and
.B tombstone
and
.B updated_at
are set to the epoch.
.PP
The reaper then picks the replica up (state
.BR B ),
"deletes" it, and removes the record.
.PP
The placeholder path is deliberate.
Rucio appends
.B path
to the RSE prefix, so the resulting PFN does not point at any real file.
This is harmless because FNAL_DCACHE is configured with Rucio's
.B mock
delete protocol: the reaper never contacts storage, and the delete always
succeeds.
Do not replace the placeholder with a real file path.
.PP
All modes are set-based.
The target DIDs are loaded into a temporary table, and each update runs
once as a join against it.
A single
.BR psql (1)
session and transaction handle any number of files.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-apply
Make the changes.
Both updates run in a single transaction with
.BR ON_ERROR_STOP ,
followed by a summary and
.BR COMMIT .
Without this option the script runs a dry run: it reports what would
change and rolls back.
.TP
.IR scope : name
Operate on a single file DID.
.TP
.BI \-\-list " file"
Read file DIDs from
.IR file ,
one
.IR scope : name
per line.
If
.I file
is
.BR \- ,
read from standard input.
Leading and trailing whitespace is trimmed, blank lines and lines starting with
.B #
are ignored, and duplicates are merged.
If any line lacks a colon, the run aborts before anything is changed.
.TP
.BI \-\-dataset " scope" : name
Operate on every file directly attached to the given dataset, looked up in the
.B contents
table
.RB ( child_type " = " 'F' ).
Files inside containers must be targeted through their datasets.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
In both modes the script prints a summary row with these columns:
.TP
.B dids
Number of distinct target DIDs.
.TP
.B replicas_on_rse
Number of those that have a replica on FNAL_DCACHE.
.TP
.B need_path
Replicas matched by update 1 (NULL path, tombstone set).
.TP
.B mark_available
Replicas matched by update 2 (unlocked, epoch tombstone).
.TP
.B locked
Replicas with
.B lock_cnt
> 0, which update 2 skips.
.PP
Up to 20 matching replica rows follow.
With
.BR \-\-apply ,
an
.BI "UPDATE " n
line is printed for each statement before the summary, and the summary
shows the state after the update.
A successful run ends with
.BR Committed. ;
if it is missing, the transaction did not commit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PGPASSWORD
Database password for user
.BR rucio .
Used if it is set; otherwise
.BR psql (1)
reads
.BR ~/.pgpass .
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.pgpass
Password file, which must have mode 0600.
Example line:
.RS
.EX
ifdb11.fnal.gov:5455:dune_rucio_prod:rucio:<password>
.EE
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Usage error, unreadable list file, or a
.BR psql (1)
internal error.
.TP
.B 2
Could not connect to the database.
.TP
.B 3
An SQL error, including malformed DIDs in a list.
The transaction is rolled back and nothing is changed.
.SH EXAMPLES
Dry run for one file:
.PP
.RS
.EX
replica_fix.sh protodune\-sp:PDSPProd4a_..._20240101T000012Z.root
.EE
.RE
.PP
Fix every file in a list:
.PP
.RS
.EX
replica_fix.sh \-\-list dids.txt
replica_fix.sh \-\-apply \-\-list dids.txt
.EE
.RE
.PP
Fix a whole dataset, checking the file count first:
.PP
.RS
.EX
rucio list\-files protodune\-sp:SOME_DATASET
replica_fix.sh \-\-dataset protodune\-sp:SOME_DATASET
replica_fix.sh \-\-apply \-\-dataset protodune\-sp:SOME_DATASET
.EE
.RE
.PP
Confirm that the reaper has removed a replica:
.PP
.RS
.EX
rucio list\-file\-replicas \-\-all\-states \fIscope\fP:\fIname\fP
.EE
.RE
.SH CAVEATS
This script writes directly to the production Rucio database, bypassing the
Rucio API.
Always run a dry run first.
.PP
With
.BR \-\-apply ,
one transaction holds row locks on every matched replica until it commits.
For very large lists, consider splitting the input into chunks of a few
thousand DIDs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR psql (1),
.BR rucio (1)
